<node id="9245">
  <data key="d0">event</data>
  <data key="d1">9245</data>
  <data key="d2">Dagstuhl Seminar</data>
  <data key="d3">Multimedia – System Architectures and Applications</data>
  <data key="d4">1992-11-02</data>
  <data key="d5">1992-11-06</data>
  <data key="d6">https://www.dagstuhl.de/9245</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">
 &lt;p&gt;The Workshop on "Multimedia--System Architectures and Applications" took place
in Schloß Dagstuhl, Germany, from November 2 to 4, 1992. There were 26
participants coming from 7 countries. The Workshop was based on presentations
(their summaries are the contents of the Dagstuhl-Seminar-Report) and three Working
Groups. The reports of these Groups are also published there. The participants
decided at the end of the Workshop that they would welcome a "follow-up
workshop" in Dagstuhl in 1994. This is now being considered.&lt;/p&gt; 
 &lt;p&gt;
As Co-Chairs of the Workshop, we would like to thank Professor Wilhelm and all
the IBFI staff in Dagstuhl for the excellent and extremely fruitful working
atmosphere which was the basis for the success of the Workshop. We also thank
all participants for their contributions and for all the very constructive discussions.
&lt;/p&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/"&gt;
&lt;img alt="Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license" src="/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/cc.png" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                        Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
  <data key="d9"></data>
  <data key="d10">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagSemRep.51</data>
  <data key="d11"></data>
  <data key="d12"></data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</node>
<node id="J. Encarnação">
  <data key="d14">J. Encarnação</data>
  <data key="d0">person</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
