&lt;/p&gt; 
 &lt;p&gt;
In computer science, the phenomena of self-reference, self-application and recursion played a crucial role in the foundational work of Gödel, Church, Turing and Kleene in the 1930s. Nevertheless, powerful mathematical models of the semantics of recursion became available only with the work of Scott on models of the untyped lambda calculus and subsequent research in domain theory. 
