                    Umberto Grandi, Stefan Napel, Rolf Niedermeier, and Kristen Brent Venable
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
  <data key="d9">https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/2020/0729.pdf; https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.08031; https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.08031; https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.00011; http://www.ifaamas.org/Proceedings/aamas2020/pdfs/p1993.pdf; https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.12104; https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-50026-9_5; https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/2020/0055.pdf; https://www.ijcai.org/Proceedings/2020/0240.pdf; https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.00161; https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.13145</data>
  <data key="d10">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.9.9.45</data>
  <data key="d11">artificial intelligence / robotics; data structures / algorithms / complexity</data>
  <data key="d12">Social Choice; Multi-Agent Systems; AI for the Social Good; Collective Decision Making</data>
